<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 2.95 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 2.95 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0830 to the dollar, up from 3.0910 on Friday and at 1.8060 to the mark, down from 1.8020, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.95 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Friday's 2.82 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
